      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "According to [[credential-scoping]], the Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment through **child-process credential injection**:\n\n1. **The Hub never holds the key**: The Hub\u0027s process environment remains clean \u2014 the key is never written into or inherited by it.\n\n2. **Load-time secrets management**: A local secrets loader reads the API key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup.\n\n3. **Child-process injection only**: The key is injected only into the environment of spawned child processes (the Ingest and Query agents) immediately before they start \u2014 not before, not shared with the Hub itself.\n\n4. **Security benefit**: This design means a compromised or misbehaving Hub process cannot leak the credential by inspecting its own environment variables. The key exists only in the short-lived child processes that actually need it to call the Anthropic API.\n\nThis pattern applies to both the Ingest and Query agents, both following the same credential scoping model.",
